  "interpretation": "The all-evidence baseline and selected scenario use the same fitted model. The intercept plus signed contributions equals the logit; applying the sigmoid gives the retrieval score, within floating-point precision. Contributions are relative to the training-feature means, so an absent feature can have a nonzero contribution. Contribution changes add in logit space, not score or probability space. A score without supporting paths is diagnostic only and has no supported rank. This is model sensitivity, not causal biological evidence or a probability of clinical efficacy."
